ID(1)                       User Commands

NAME
    id, whoami, groups - print user and group identities

SYNOPSIS
    id [-u | -g | -G] [-n] [user]
    whoami
    groups [user...]

DESCRIPTION
    id prints the real user and group ids of the calling process with
    their account names, the effective ids when they differ, and the
    supplementary groups. With a user argument it prints the ids that
    account receives at login from /etc/passwd and /etc/group.

    -u prints only the effective uid, -g only the effective gid and -G
    only the group list. -n prints names instead of numbers with these
    options.

    whoami prints the account name of the effective uid.

    groups prints the group names of the calling process, or of each named
    account, with the primary group first.

FILES
    /etc/passwd, /etc/group

SEE ALSO
    ps(1), passwd(5), index(7)
